alexander dugan listening to tributes to  his daughter  daria dugina was killed on saturday in a  car bomb attack near moscow her father  says she recently told him she felt like  a warrior  the price that we have to pay can be  justified by only one thing the highest  achievement victory she lived in the  name of victory and she died in the name  of victory our russian victory our truth  our orthodoxy our country and our empire  daria dugina was 29 and worked as a  commentator on a nationalist russian  television channel just two days after  the attack russia's federal security  service or fsb named a ukrainian woman  as the perpetrator it said she'd rented  an apartment in the same building as  dugina  ukraine has said it does not resort to  terror tactics blaming russia's own  government or security apparatus it  typically takes months or even years or  often never  for uh political murders to be solved  and yet uh the fsb the russian security  service claims to have done this in a  matter of hours and i think everyone  looking at the kind of details they're  providing  you come to the conclusion there's  nothing credible about the story that  they have put together  how much influence dugan has over  president vladimir putin has been the  subject of speculation inside and  outside russia  what's clear is he and his daughter  expressed far-right nationalist views in  public and strongly supported the  invasion of ukraine they'd both been  placed on international sanctions lists  for spreading misinformation  witnesses say alexander dugan decided at  the last minute to travel in a different  vehicle from his daughter  social media footage showed him looking  on with the car still in flames  president putin has never publicly  supported him but he's called the car  bomb evil and posthumously awarded  dugina the order of courage medal nadeem  baba al-jazeera
 

